14e9768:d00\", \"start\": 462, \"end\": 503, \"text\": \"He served ten consecutive two-year terms.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d00\", \"start\": 504, \"end\": 542, \"text\": \"Late in his life, he moved to Chicago.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d00\", \"start\": 543, \"end\": 566, \"text\": \"Dailey married Clara F.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d00\", \"start\": 567, \"end\": 584, \"text\": \"Johnston, a music\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 607, \"text\": \"from Niagara Falls , New York People from Lewiston , New York Republican Party New York ( state ) state senators Fordham University alumni University of Iowa alumni Harvard Business School alumni Republican Party members of the New York State Assembly State cabinet secretaries of New York ( state ) People from Woodside , Queens 20th-century members of the New York State Legislature Hidden categories : CS1 maint : multiple names : authors list Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata S-bef : 'before ' parameter begins with the word 'new ' Template : Succession box :\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 79, \"text\": \"[ 42 ] [ 43 ] [ 44 ] [ 45 ] Daley's campaign placed an emphasis on fundraising.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 80, \"end\": 129, \"text\": \"[ 46 ] Daley vastly out-fundraised his opponents.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 130, \"end\": 221, \"text\": \"A significant financial contributor to Daley's campaign was Illinois billionaire Kenneth C.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 222, \"end\": 230, \"text\": \"Griffin.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 231, \"end\": 472, \"text\": \"[ 47 ] Griffin's financial support of Daley's campaign proved controversial for Daley, largely because Griffin had also been a major financial backer of the failed 2018 reelection campaign of Republican former Illinois governor Bruce Rauner.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"start\": 473, \"end\": 623, \"text\": \"[ 46 ] Daley's strong fundraising enabled him to run highly visible advertising, which helped solidify his position as a leading Democratic candidate.\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 428, \"text\": \"Noam Chomsky Judy Collins Bernardine Dohrn Allen Ginsberg Judy Gumbo Anita Hoffman Paul Krassner Nancy Kurshan Timothy Leary Norman Mailer Country Joe McDonald Graham Nash Phil Ochs Pigasus Ed Sanders Context Youth International Party ( Yippies ) 1968 Democratic National Convention protests `` The whole world is watching `` Counterculture of the 1960s National Mobilization Committee to End the War in Vietnam Mayor Richard J.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d03\", \"start\": 429, \"end\": 608, \"text\": \"Daley Vietnam War opposition Miami and the Siege of Chicago ( 1968 book ) Weather Underground Media `` Chicago '' ( 1970 song ) Conspiracy : The Trial of the Chicago 8 ( 1987 film\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 392, \"text\": \", 2025 Wisconsin Supreme Court elections , 2025 2024 general election voter turnout Ballotpedia News Public Policy Administrative state Criminal justice policy Education policy Environmental , social , and corporate governance ( ESG ) Federalism Unemployment insurance Work requirements Policy in the states Information for candidates Ballotpedia 's Candidate Survey How do I run for office ?\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d04\", \"start\": 393, \"end\": 417, \"text\": \"How do I update a page ?\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d04\", \"start\": 418, \"end\": 680, \"text\": \"Election results Send us candidate contact info Get Engaged Donate to Ballotpedia Contact us Report an error Events Newsletters Ballotpedia Podcast Careers Volunteer Ad Policy Ballotpedia Boutique Services Media inquiries Data sales API Premium Research Services\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Dailey\", \"scope\": \"Political party affiliation\", \"claim\": \"Dailey was elected as Republican to the Illinois House of Representatives.\", \"answer\": \"Republican\", \"quote\": \"Also that year, Dailey was elected as Republican to the Illinois House of Representatives, serving a two-year term.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0082-aecc414e9768:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Dailey\", \"scope\": \"Political affiliation\", \"claim\": \"Daley's strong fundraising enabled him to run highly visible advertising, which helped solidify his position as a leading Democratic candidate.\", \"answer\": \"Democratic\", \"quote\": \"[ 46 ] Daley's strong fundraising enabled him to run highly visible advertising, which helped solidify his position as a leading Democratic candidate.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Republican\", \"Democratic\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Democratic\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Republican\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
